__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# data/ is an ALLOWLIST, not a denylist. The workflow commits with `git add -A`,
# so a future credential file (data/creds.env, data/token.txt, ...) would be
# swept into this PUBLIC repo automatically. Only these three state files ship;
# anything else added under data/ is ignored by default and must be opted in.
data/*
!data/latest.json
!data/smallcap.json
!data/screen_log.json
!data/portfolio.json
# NOTE: every file the system must REMEMBER between runs has to be listed here.
# The cloud starts from a fresh checkout each time, so an un-listed state file
# is silently recreated from scratch on every run and never accumulates.

# private research workspace living inside this public repo — NEVER commit
Small Cap Research/

# a local slot for previewing states the live data does not currently
# show (e.g. the books mid-run before they have opened). Never shipped.
site/_preview.html

# --- credential catch-all ---
# The data/ allowlist above covers data/*.key, but a key pasted ANYWHERE else
# — a root .env, a scratch file, a config dir — would be swept in by
# `git add -A`. This repo is PUBLIC and that has already happened once: two
# live keys were committed, the history had to be rewritten and both keys
# rotated. These patterns are deliberately broad. Comments must be on their
# own line: git treats a trailing "# ..." as part of the pattern.
.env
*.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*credentials*
*secret*
*token*

